@flexiarg pattern-interpretation/put-uncertainty-in-theta
@title Put Real Uncertainty In θ And C, Not In Unknown Facts
@keywords theta, prior, outcome, want, coverage, observation, preference
@audience interpretation jobs, cascade-model builders
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-16 (claude-7; findings F2, F3; claude-4 agreed to make attested θ required (D6) and to score want coverage on predicted observation (D7))
@references [pattern-interpretation/declare-the-universe pattern-interpretation/compile-guards-exactly translation/declare-what-is-lost]
@see-also buffer-cleaner/classify-staleness
@why prose patterns carry uncertainty about the world ("will this buffer be needed later?") and name outcomes no act directly produces ("clean enough", "repo clean"). Encoding the first as an unknown fact makes the pattern never fire; leaving the second as an effect-less want makes coverage zero on every path.
@how a prior about the world becomes the attested θ of the acting pattern (the probability its effect is achieved) or part of C, never a guard over an :unknown fact. A want that is a world outcome is added as a θ-weighted effect of the pattern whose act brings it about, and coverage is scored on the predicted observation of that token, so a fix that is confirmed only by the next tick's observation is counted as predicted, not as done.
@violation-signature a guard NOT needed-later that can never fire; θ left at the documented default 1 for an outcome with a declared prior; want coverage computed over produced tokens at θ = 1.
! conclusion: World uncertainty lives in θ or C, outcome wants are θ-weighted effects scored on predicted observation, and unknown is kept for unobserved facts.

  + context: Flexiargs such as buffer-cleaner/classify-staleness state priors (temp 0.05, dired 0.25, file-stale 0.40 at 6 h).

  + IF:
    A pattern's prose expresses uncertainty about outcomes or names a goal state.

  + HOWEVER:
    The guard language is logical and the effect language is add-only and certain.

  + THEN:
    Move priors into θ or C and give outcome wants a θ-weighted producing effect scored by observation.

  + BECAUSE:
    Guards decide whether an act may happen; θ and C decide what it is expected to achieve and how much that is wanted.

  + evidence: worked instances §1 (clean-enough never produced), §2 (repo-clean likewise); claude-4's tick-1 observation that "partial summary observes cleanly" is established by the fix but confirmed only at the next tick.
